  "openLibrarySub": "Books, authors and full-text search",
  "helpHowTitle": "How Manabi works",
  "helpHowBody": "1. It understands your question and writes Arabic search terms.\n2. It searches thousands of Turath books, including any school or book you name.\n3. It reads the most relevant pages and picks the best ones.\n4. It writes the answer from those pages only.\n5. Every quoted passage is matched word for word against the book; anything not found is removed.",
  "helpTipsTitle": "Tips for a good question",
  "helpTipsBody": "• Ask a clear, specific question.\n• If you want a school's view, name it (Hanafi, Shafi'i, Maliki, Hanbali).\n• Name a book, or use + to limit the search to a book, author or category.\n• Choose Deep research for difficult or disputed questions.",
  "helpSourcesTitle": "Sources and citations",
  "helpSourcesBody": "The Sources button under every answer lists each citation: book, author, volume, page, the original Arabic text and a direct link on Turath. Small numbers like [1] in the text point to that source.",
  "helpLimitsTitle": "Limits",
  "helpLimitsBody": "Manabi is not a mufti; it reports what the books say, and says so plainly when it finds no documented answer. For a ruling on your own situation, consult a trusted scholar.",
  "privacyStoredTitle": "What is stored",
  "privacyStoredBody": "Your chats, saved answers and settings are kept on your device only. Manabi needs no account and collects no personal data.",
  "privacySentTitle": "What is sent",
  "privacySentBody": "When you ask, the question and a short summary of recent answers are sent to the Manabi server (or to Google Gemini in direct mode) to build the answer, and search terms are sent to turath.io. The server does not store questions; it keeps an answer in memory for up to 20 minutes so an interrupted answer can be recovered.",
  "privacyKeyTitle": "Your key",
  "privacyKeyBody": "If you use your own Gemini key, it is kept in the device's secure storage (Keychain / Keystore) and sent only to Google.",
  "privacyDeleteTitle": "Deleting",
  "privacyDeleteBody": "You can delete all chats and settings at any time under Data & storage.",
